First, before you attempt to read the genocide scroll.  Find out if it is
cursed, uncursed, or blessed.  The effects are fatally different.

Cursed
------
Wraiths - experience levels
Dragons of your choice - intrinsic
Minotaurs - wand of digging

Uncursed (or unknown)
----------------------
You should always try to curse or bless the genocide before using it,
except in some very limited cases.

However for some reason, you read one that is uncursed(or unknown), you
should try something moderate, it will niether kill you or give you a
lot of advantage.  You can always know a genocide scroll is blessed since
it asks you for a class of monster instead of a single one.  Do it in
a corridor so you can suffer less per turn if the scroll happens to be
cursed.

Case : Unknown
--------------
Rust monster - there is only one monster in the rust monster class, the
               rust monster itself.  There is no different for using a
               blessed scroll or an uncursed scroll.


Case : Uncursed
---------------
Titans - you don't want to genocide the whole class of giants.  Since
         Titans can cast nasty spells and eating them do not give you
         extra strength, it wise to eliminate them.

Soldier ants - Deadly for lower level characters.  Again you don't want
               to eliminate the whole class of insect.


Blessed
-------
Lich - deadly class of monster you never want to encounter.



